STEP 1: Login to AWS
Open AWS
Open Chrome browser
Go to: https://aws.amazon.com
Click: Sign In to Console

You can find this button at the top-right corner.

Enter:
Email
Password
Click: Sign In

Now you will see the AWS Dashboard.

STEP 2: Open VPC Service
Search for VPC
At the top of AWS page, you will see a search bar.
Click the search bar.
Type: VPC
Click the service named: VPC

Now VPC Dashboard opens.

STEP 3: Create a VPC
Where is the Button?

On left side menu:

Click: Your VPCs

At top-right:

Click orange button: Create VPC
Fill Details

Choose:

VPC only

Enter:

Field	Value
Name tag	Custom-VPC
IPv4 CIDR	10.0.0.0/16
IPv6 CIDR	No IPv6 CIDR Block
Tenancy	Default

After filling:

Click orange button: Create VPC

You will see:

“Successfully created VPC”
STEP 4: Create Public Subnet
Open Subnets

Left side menu:

Click: Subnets

Top-right:

Click: Create subnet
Fill Public Subnet Details
Select VPC

Click dropdown under:

VPC ID

Select:

Custom-VPC
Subnet Settings
Field	Value
Subnet name	Public-Subnet
Availability Zone	ap-south-1a
IPv4 CIDR block	10.0.1.0/24

Now click:

Create subnet

Public subnet created.

STEP 5: Create Private Subnet

Again click:

Create subnet

Fill:

Field	Value
Subnet name	Private-Subnet
Availability Zone	ap-south-1a
IPv4 CIDR block	10.0.2.0/24

Click:

Create subnet

Private subnet created.

STEP 6: Create Internet Gateway (IGW)
Open Internet Gateways

Left menu:

Click: Internet Gateways

Top-right:

Click: Create internet gateway
Fill Details
Field	Value
Name tag	My-IGW

Click:

Create internet gateway
STEP 7: Attach IGW to VPC

After creating:

Select checkbox beside My-IGW
Top-right click: Actions
Click: Attach to VPC

A popup opens.

Select: Custom-VPC
Click: Attach internet gateway

Done.

STEP 8: Create Public Route Table
Open Route Tables

Left menu:

Click: Route Tables

Top-right:

Click: Create route table
Fill Details
Field	Value
Name	Public-RT
VPC	Custom-VPC

Click:

Create route table
STEP 9: Add Internet Route
Select Public-RT
Bottom section tabs appear
Click: Routes tab
Click: Edit routes
Click: Add route

Fill:

Destination	Target
0.0.0.0/0	Internet Gateway

Then select:

My-IGW

Now click:

Save changes
STEP 10: Associate Public Subnet
Open Public-RT
Click tab: Subnet associations
Click: Edit subnet associations
Tick checkbox: Public-Subnet
Click: Save associations

Done.

STEP 11: Launch EC2 Instance
Open EC2 Service

Top search bar:

Type: EC2

Click:

EC2
Launch Instance
Left menu click: Instances
Top-right click orange button: Launch instances
STEP 12: Configure EC2
Instance Name

Under Name:

Enter: MyServer
Choose AMI

Under:

Amazon Machine Image (AMI)

Select:

Amazon Linux 2 AMI
Instance Type

Select:

t2.micro

Free tier eligible.

STEP 13: Create Key Pair
Where?

Scroll to:

Key pair section

Click:

Create new key pair
Fill Details
Field	Value
Key pair name	my-key
Key pair type	RSA
Private key format	.pem

Click:

Create key pair

Important:

PEM file downloads automatically.
Do NOT delete it.
Store safely.
STEP 14: Network Settings

In Network settings:

Click:

Edit

Fill:

Setting	Value
VPC	Custom-VPC
Subnet	Public-Subnet
Auto-assign Public IP	Enable
Security Group Rules

Allow SSH:

Type	Port	Source
SSH	22	Anywhere
STEP 15: Launch Instance

Review everything.

Now click orange button:

Launch instance

Wait few seconds.

You will see:

“Successfully launched instance”
STEP 16: Connect to EC2 Instance
Open Instance
Click: View all instances
Select your instance checkbox.
Connect Button

Top-right click:

Connect

You will see multiple tabs.

Click:

EC2 Instance Connect

Then click orange button:

Connect

A terminal opens.

Congratulations. You are now connected to Linux server.

STEP 17: Test Commands

Inside terminal type:

pwd

Press Enter.

Then:

ls

Then:

sudo yum update -y
OUTPUT

You successfully:

Created VPC
Created Public & Private Subnets
Attached Internet Gateway
Configured Route Table
Launched EC2 Instance
Connected to EC2 Server
